<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto#"
     xml:base="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:obo="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
     xmlns:heto="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_"
     xmlns:oheo="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/OHEO_"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:rheo="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/RHEO_"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
     xmlns:heto1="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:oboInOwl="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/0.3.0/heto.owl"/>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Baines D, Ashley M. Health Economics Task Ontology (HETO), version 0.2.0, for BioPortal. Intelligent Parameters Ltd; 2026. https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/0.3.0/heto.owl. Licence CC BY 4.0.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-17</dcterms:created>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678"/>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731"/>
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">HETO, the Health Economics Task Ontology, describes recognisable units of health economics work, such as adding discounting to an economic model or running a probabilistic sensitivity analysis, and connects each one to the real things it works on, as RHEO and OHEO define them. A HETO task is a reusable specification of a defined unit of work. It states an intended result and the main actions directed towards it, independently of any particular practitioner, project or software. Following the Information Artifact Ontology, a task specification is a plan specification (IAO_0000104) with an objective specification and action specifications as parts. Each named task in the pilot catalogue is an individual with its own URI; subclasses of task specification classify kinds of task. A particular performance of the work is a separate planned process (health economics task performance), linked to the specification it follows by &apos;specified by information&apos; (RO_0017010), as Duncan et al. 2024 recommend. Three relations are kept apart. Classification (rdf:type) says what kind of task something is; decomposition (has subtask specification) says which smaller tasks make up a larger one; ordering (normally precedes) says which work is usually done first. Policy (decided by Darrin Baines, 17 October 2026). HEO is a thesaurus of concepts, which are not real things; RHEO and OHEO define the real things of health economics within BFO 2020; HETO describes work on those real things, so its logical links go to RHEO and OHEO only. Each task names the RHEO or OHEO types of its inputs, outputs and processes, and the HETO role of the person who does it. HEO concepts are not linked from heto.ttl. They appear only in heto-mappings.sssom.tsv, as secondary skos:relatedMatch rows for learning and navigation, which state no requirement and no identity. No HETO class uses a HEO concept URI. Requirements on the catalogue and on records of task performances are SHACL shapes in heto-shapes.ttl.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-17</dcterms:issued>
        <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
        <dcterms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-20</dcterms:modified>
        <dcterms:publisher>Intelligent Parameters Ltd</dcterms:publisher>
        <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">Health Economics Task Ontology (HETO)</dcterms:title>
        <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>heto</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
        <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto/HETO_</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Pilot release (status alpha) for review by its creators and invited reviewers before the task list is expanded. HETO imports RHEO 0.4.0 with its uncertainty module and OHEO 0.3.0, and through them BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2); the BFO, IAO, COB, OBI and RO terms RHEO declares are not declared again. The other reused terms (IAO objective specification and action specification, RO has part, information specifies and specified by information, OBI achieves planned objective) are declared with their official label and definition as served by the EBI Ontology Lookup Service on 2026-10-16 (IAO 2026-03-30, RO 2026-09-04, OBI 2026-07-27), with one parent the source asserts where it asserts one. Consult the source ontologies for their full axioms. This file, heto-0.3.0-merged.owl, is the file for BioPortal. It is heto.ttl without its import statements, merged by ROBOT with a BOT extract of the external terms HETO uses from RHEO 0.4.0 (with its uncertainty module), OHEO 0.3.0 and BFO 2020, each extracted term marked with the ontology that defines it, so that BioPortal lists HETO&apos;s own terms and not the whole of RHEO and OHEO. For the full ontology with its imports, load heto.owl.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heo"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo"/>
        <owl:versionInfo>0.3.0 (alpha)</owl:versionInfo>
        <foaf:homepage rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heto"/>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


